2nd barbarian ascension.

Only 2 deaths between my last ascension(v3 the Valk), feeling great
about that!
Once again, good luck shined on this character.  On dlvl2, found a
shop containing 3 lamps, one of which was magic.  Picked up some dwarf
mithril and other dwarf armor on the way to Minetown.  For the first
time in a long time, Minetown altar was co-aligned.  If I recall
correctly, the deli had only 1 item, a water potion.  A pray, bless,
and a rub later, and I had GDSM.I was not ready to hit mine's end yet,
but I did find a long sword so I could train up.  I got my wish there,
it was cursed.  Crom saw fit to uncurse it after a few prayers.

On dlvl6, found a bones file of a fairly well equipped Valk that
apparently fell into a poisoned spike trap.  Found Excalibur,
gauntlets of dexterity, bad of tricks, and a BoH!  Not too shabby.
Sokoban yielded amulet of reflection as well.  Good thing too, as the
big room, just a level or two below had a baddie with a death wand.
Yoink!

Back at minetown, the bag of tricks helped me get Cleaver.  Mine's end
was the cellar, which netted me plenty of booze to convert to water.
A dwarf beat me to the luckstone(and gems).  I retrieved them from his
corpse, but not before he had picked up other gray stones.  Jerk.

Further down I found out that religion was very popular in this
dungeon.  At least 6 altars spread out, 3 co-aligned, and two had
priests(1 co-aligned).  I have never seen multiple multiple altars on
one level.  This game had two such levels.  Sac fest produced fire
brand.  At that point I did some alchemy to whittle down the potions.
First game I can remember where full healing was smokey.  Another wish
later and I had speed boots.

Before moving further down, I always like to max out my protection.  I
found Ludios on dlvl 11 or 12 I think, first try.  Like my last
ascension, a cockatrice came out as one of the first in the zoo and
left a corpse.  50 statues later and I had cleared out the outer
areas.  I had no means of levitation, so I froze the moat and cleared
out the level, and shortly after, maxed out protection.

I got a little greedy and starting another sac fest after polypiling
some magical tools I had.  No markers. :(  I did get some bag of
tricks, so I used them.  I guess I forgot that were creatures are
human and lost protection(and was cursed, and got my altar converted,
and all sorts of other bad things).  Luckily I bought all my
protection from a cross-aligned priest.  I polymorphed him into an ant
and took my money back, re-investing it at the minetown priest.  Oddly
enough, no punishment from the dead priest's(ant's) god.  I did the
quest at that point.  Nothing interesting happened there.

I cruised through Medusa, using the scimitar for dual wielding(to get
skill up).  I foolishly invoked my artifact to float around the castle
and then set myself down for some reason.  I think I floated around
that way because gremlins were generated near the moat and were
getting out of hand.  I was then stuck trying to avoid the trap
doors.  I ended up icing the moat and playing mastermind(for the first
time ever) for castle entrance.  I smashed most of the baddies in the
gate, then wiped up the rest.  The wand was fully charged.  I wished
for gauntlets of power and a magic marker.  I enchanted up my good
equipment to get me to about -33 AC.

In the valley, I found a katana and enchanted it up to +7, thinking it
was a pretty good find.  A few turns later, a silver spear turned up,
and later some siler sabers.  I just stuck it out with +6 Firebrand
and +7 katana through the game.  I never found genocide, so I wished
for some scrolls and wiped out L and V.  I later wished for another
marker and genocided R and m(before Orcus).  I was really surprised
how hard I was hitting since I haven't two-weaponed in a while.  Lots
of 1 turn kills.  Not too far down, someone dropped a magic lamp,
which I kept for light.  I killed Jubilex before he could engulf me,
which was nice.

Again, it got rediculous, as I found a wand of wishing randomly
towards the end of the hell.  I ran into some trouble after eating a
chameleon, which I thought was a crocodile.  Broke my cloak and ended
up trapped between a disenchanter and a mastadon.  One way or another
I got out of that pickle and was transformed back.  Wished up a new
cloak and enchanted my armor until it was satisfactory.  More alchemy
produced another wish, which I used to get a ring of levitation, the
only reliable source found in that game.  Also, a succubus released
another djinni from a smokey potion after I whacked him.

Marked the square and killed the wizard, who was holding a blessed
magic lamp of all things.  The santum was much improved over my last
run.  I used speed and power to strike down the priests and other
summoners before they could fill up the sanctum.  Easy pickins.
Mysterious force was tolerable, no real trouble on the way up.  Used
gold detection and confusion potions to cruise through the plains.  I
again took Pestilence(rgrn apparently does not agree).  It was
lawful.  Death had already broken through the middle door.  I felled
him in 3 hits, and he got 1 in on me.  Waltzed up and found the
neutral altar!

